# The negation of an interval of the round-up interval (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Sum,
# difference, negation"): the two lanes exchanged, -[a, b] = [-b, -a] stored as (a, -b); exact, in
# every rounding mode; the empty set stays empty. Requires the rounding mode upward set by
# kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math,
# MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_neg_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        pair z = zu zn
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       encloses_interval zu zn -x x=xu,xn tight=exact bounded_when=abs_le(-x,omega) bounded_exactly
min_precision: 1
source:        the two lanes exchanged (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardArith.v upward_neg_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the lanes exchanged, each a bound of its own; encloses_interval states what comes out for every canonical state

zu = copy(xn) | zn = copy(xu)                   # swap(x)
